==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Old English [[misteltan|misteltān]], from [[mistel]] ‘mistletoe’ + [[tan#Old English|tān]] ‘twig’.  Compare [[mistle]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmɪsəltəʊ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several parasitic [[evergreen]] plants with white [[berry|berries]] that grow in the crowns of [[oak]]s, apple trees and other trees.
# A [[sprig]] of these plants used as a [[Christmas]] [[decoration]].

====Usage notes====
The term '''mistletoe''' is used for both {{taxlink|Viscum album|species}} ([[European mistletoe]]) and {{taxlink|Phoradendron leucarpum|species}} ([[eastern mistletoe]]).

====Derived terms====
* [[mistletoebird]]

